ailor/eecdce4d-f714-4989-9c7e-75d34df59560", "location": "Remote (North America)", "posted": "2026-09-22T22:06:25.700+00:00", "external_id": "eecdce4d-f714-4989-9c7e-75d34df59560", "description": "ABOUT TAILOR\n\nTailor is a pioneer in Headless ERP technology. Our platform empowers companies to build internal workflows that adapt to their unique needs \u2014 faster, smarter, and developer-first.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe're looking for an Associate Forward-Deployed Product Manager to own the day-to-day execution of live client implementations. You'll be the first line of communication with our clients and the person keeping the project moving \u2014 coordinating directly with the internal development team, tracking progress and blockers, running testing and training, and making sure what was committed is what gets delivered. You'll work collaboratively with the Account Manager and Senior PM (Forward-Deployed Product Manager), who own the commercial relationship and solution design; you own the execution.\n\nThis is a development role designed to grow into the Senior PM role. Progression is based on performance and can be accelerated accordingly.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own Day-to-Day Client Communications \u2014 Manage day-to-day client communications, including question handling, escalation management, and requests to the client, keeping clients informed and unblocked.\n\n - Drive Project Execution & Tracking \u2014 Run the execution rhythm of the project: coordinate with the internal development team, maintain project management tools (e.g., GitHub Projects, Jira), and keep status, documentation, and release notes current for internal and client teams.\n\n - Client Data & Gap Analysis \u2014 Analyze client data to surface gaps, discrepancies, and risks, and support the Senior PM and engineering in solution architecture and functional gap analysis.\n\n - Testing, Coordination & Go-Live Prep \u2014 Validate every release before it reaches the client, coordinate client testing and sign-off, and own go-live readiness. Testing is how we protect client trust \u2014 it is a core part of this role.\n\n - Client Training & Enablement \u2014 Create training materials and deliver training so client teams are set up to operate the platform independently.\n\n - Influence the Platform Roadmap \u2014 Develop deep knowledge of the Tailor platform and translate client feedback into product insights that inform the roadmap.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2\u20135 years of experience in product management in either big tech or a startup, and/or management consulting experience; management consulting strongly preferred\n\n - Proven customer-facing experience, comfortable in front of both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Sharp, structured thinker who is comfortable with ambiguity and eager to learn and grow\n\n - Ownership mindset with an appetite for operational and technical detail\n\n - Exceptional written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Comfortable with data analysis tools and AI-driven workflows\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - You build things in your spare time \u2014 show us a side project you've vibe coded and walk us through how you approached it\n\n - Exposure to ecommerce or physical-product operations \u2014 order, inventory, purchasing, fulfillment, or accounting workflows\n\n - Familiarity with ERP, 3PL, or commerce platforms\n\n - Prior experience onboarding customers onto software\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION & BENEFITS\n\n - Salary: USD 100,000 to USD 130,000 yearly\n\n - Benefits: Health, dental, vision, flexible PTO, and more\n\n\n\n\nWHY TAILOR?\n\nYou'll work directly with the product team on a fast-growing platform solving real operational pain. If you love being the voice of the customer, reducing friction, and making teams more effective \u2014 let's talk. Apply now and help us shape the future of Headless ERP.\n\n", "extra": {"department": "US", "team": "US", "compensation": "$100K \u2013 $130K \u2022 Benefits: Gym and office stipends, plus comprehensive health and dental insurance."}, "group": "startup", "investor": "Y Combinator", "ats": "ashby"}]}